! mcp_bootstrap_p134.strap -- the Y INTERRUPT-NAME TABLE and
! "***** SPECIAL INTERRUPT ROUTINE FOR TS *****", printed page 134.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.141 (printed + 7).  THE HEADER WAS
! READ, NOT ASSUMED: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID
! 11011MCP   CARD ID ED000153   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER
! 134", rendered on its own at 600 dpi.
!
! FIFTY LINES, AND NONE WERE LOST OFF EITHER END.  The card-serial
! column runs ED000153 (line 1) to ED000202 (line 50) without a gap
! -- 153 + 49 = 202 -- so line n carries serial ED000(152+n) and the
! render covers the whole page.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS, IN TWO HALVES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-29 are a TABLE OF INTERRUPT-INDICATOR NAMES: a CNOP, then
! twenty-seven "(AA)DD(BU,32),xxxx A" entry-mode cards, one per 7030
! indicator, then a second CNOP.  Each card is named YIN** and
! reserves one half word; the datum is the indicator's own mnemonic
! as four characters of the 48 Character Set (STRAP entry mode A,
! terminated by "A" -- C28-6129 printed p.16: the second character
! of the entry-mode field is the end-of-statement character and is
! not compiled, so "(AA)" is mode A terminated by A).
!
! Lines 30-32 are three definitions (YSFIC, YSFBCR, YSFLOR), lines
! 33-34 a comment box, and lines 35-50 the sixteen instructions of
! the special-interrupt routine JWLODE.
!
! >>> THE BINARY OUTPUT COLUMN IS EMPTY ON LINES 2-28. <<<  Checked
! at 900 dpi over the whole column, not inferred from the 400-dpi
! page: the entry-mode DD cards print a LOCATION and a NAME and
! nothing else, where the two CNOPs around them print
! "000000.30 00".  So those twenty-seven rows can carry a !SYM and
! can NOT carry a !CHECK -- there is no printed word to compare the
! thirty-two assembled bits against.  Their datum rests on the ink
! and on the corroboration below, never on an oracle.
!
! THE TWENTY-SEVEN NAMES ARE SETTLED BY A TABLE, NOT BY INK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every datum is a 7030 INDICATOR MNEMONIC and strap/opcodes.py's
! INDICATOR_BITS (Reference Manual Figure 11) gives them with their
! bit numbers:  DF 20, IF 21, LC 22, PF 23, ZD 24, IR 25, LS 26,
! PSH 27, XPFP 28, XPO 29, XPH 30, XPL 31, XPU 32, ZM 33, RU 34,
! TF 35, UF 36, VF 37, XF 38, BTR 39, DTR 40, PG0..PG6 41-47.
! The page's data, in printed order, are
!   DF LC PF ZD IR LS PSH XPFP XPO XPH XPL ZM RU TF UF VF XF BTR
!   DTR PG0 PG1 PG2 PG3 PG4 PG5 PG6 XPU
! -- the indicator list in bit order with IF (21) omitted and XPU
! (32) moved to the end.  So LC really is a C (Lost Carry), ZD is a
! D (Zero Divisor), XPO is an O (eXPonent Overflow) and PG0 ends in
! a DIGIT zero, and none of the four rests on this drum.  Line 9's
! datum really is the four letters XPFP, not XPF padded: the column
! measurement below puts a glyph in all four datum positions.
!
! A SECOND, INDEPENDENT READING OF THESE ADDRESSES ALREADY EXISTS,
! AND IT COVERS ALL TWENTY-SEVEN.  printed p.114's lines 11-47 are
! "LVI,$1,YIN**; B,YMSF" pairs and printed p.115 continues them, so
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p114.strap and p115.strap between them SYN
! every YIN** name off this page.  Run through
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py with this deck added, all
! twenty-seven names group at exactly the bit this page prints --
! DF..BTR and XPU from p.114, DTR and PG0..PG6 from p.115 --
! including YINXPU at 216603.00, out of bit order.  YSFIC agrees
! with p.110's deck and JWLODE with p.112's.  Nothing here was
! changed to match any of them; the whole run is 0 hits over 1143
! name groups.
!
! THE DATUM FIELD WAS MEASURED, NOT EYEBALLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "Is the terminator one column further right on lines 2 and 3?"
! could not be answered by looking.  The statement column was
! rendered at 900 dpi and the ink profiled by column: the character
! pitch is 91 px, "(AA)DD(BU,32)," occupies cells 1-14, the datum
! occupies cells 15-18 on EVERY one of the twenty-seven cards, and
! the terminator A sits in cell 19 on every one.  What the eye saw
! as "further right" was the datum's own alignment:
!
!   cells 15-18 = "DF  " "LC  " on lines 2 and 3  (LEFT-aligned)
!   cells 15-18 = " PF " " ZD " " IR " " LS "     (one blank in front)
!   cells 15-18 = " PSH" " XPO" ... " XPU"        (three letters)
!   cells 15-18 = "XPFP"                          (four letters)
!
! The keypunch was inconsistent and the assembler does not care: all
! six shapes assemble to exactly 32 bits, measured by putting a
! named VF after each and reading the symbol table.  The datum IS
! transcribed as printed anyway, because nothing checks it.
!
! THE JOINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE TOP OF THIS PAGE IS NOT CLOSED, AND THE SLC BELOW IS AN
! ASSERTION. <<<  The page prints no SLC of its own and printed
! p.133 is not transcribed, so "SLC,(8)216565.40" states the
! arriving counter rather than checking it.  A hard SLC overrides
! the counter silently (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "WHAT THE
! ORACLE CANNOT SEE", item 2), so every !CHECK below would still
! pass if this origin were wrong.  What is known about the join:
! printed p.133's last card is line 51, "216563.70 * YMIMIC
! (AX)DD(BU), X", and line 1 here is a CNOP at 216565.40.  Thirteen
! characters of YMIMIC's datum fit that gap exactly (216565.40 -
! 216563.70 = 104 bits = 13 eight-bit bytes), which is consistent
! but is NOT a check; p.133 has to land before the top is closed.
!
! >>> THE BOTTOM IS CLOSED, BY THE NEXT PAGE'S OWN ASSEMBLER. <<<
! printed p.135 line 8 prints "216620.40 *  SLC,$" (PDF p.142, read
! at 600 dpi, not taken from the OCR).  An SLC emits nothing, so its
! printed LOCATION *is* the counter arriving from this page -- and
! line 50 here is "B,KSUPP" at 216620.00, one half word earlier.
! The two agree.  No !CHECK can consume that, so it is recorded in
! the note on line 50 instead.
!
! TAIL SCOPE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the origin, and
! pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block that printed p.2 opened
! and printed p.98 line 37 closed.  So YUXSAV here is 231363.00
! while the YUXSAV of printed p.37 is 002324.00.  Two different
! names in two different tails, NOT a collision, and not reconciled.
!
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every one of the fifty line numbers carries the ordinary trailing
! asterisk ("1*", "50*"); that is the column, not a mark.  LINES 20
! AND 42 carry a SECOND asterisk after the LOCATION -- "216577.00 *"
! and "216612.40 *" -- the familiar mark printed pp.3/37/38/39/88/
! 97/98/104 also carry.  It changes no compiled bit; both rows are
! checked below and both pass.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED AWAY FROM THE DRUM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * Line 30's statement reads "VF,C" to the eye.  It is VF,0: the
!   row's own BINARY OUTPUT is "000000.00+", and listing_oracle
!   renders a VF as a 24-bit value plus its sign, so the operand is
!   the value zero.  (The page prints 0 as an open C constantly --
!   line 1's own binary reads "CCCCCC.3C CO" at 400 dpi.)
! * Line 38's mnemonic reads BOPZ here and BCPZ in the volume OCR.
!   It is BOPZ.  The OCR of this listing carries the same card six
!   times with the same comment "-FOR LASL LRL" and the same byte
!   C6, four times as BOPZ and twice as BCPZ, and dropout opens a
!   closed glyph but never closes an open one.  Decided, not by the
!   count, but by strap_asm: BOPZ assembles to the printed
!   "216607.47 C6" and BCPZ is rejected as an unknown mnemonic.
! * Lines 31-32's names end "CR", not "DR".  The letters are round
!   with no left stem where SBNDRS on the same row prints a D with
!   a straight vertical left stem, and the volume OCR corroborates
!   YSFBCR twice in English: printed p.132 "LX,$3,YSFBCR  -RESET
!   BOUNDARY CONTROL" and printed p.133 "LX,$L,YSFBCR  SET NEW
!   BOUNDARY CONTROL".  BCR is the Boundary Control Register.
!   >>> YSFLOR, NOT YSFLCR (settled 2026-11-06). <<<  The assembler's
!   own "SYMBOLS NEVER USED IN PROGRAM", printed p.442 row 4, prints
!   "YSFLOR 231363.00" with a CLOSED O; this label's open glyph says
!   nothing on this drum (tests/check_never_used_symbols.py).  What
!   follows was written when the C rested on this page alone:
!   >>> YSFLCR IS THE ONE NAME ON THIS PAGE WITH NO OUTSIDE
!   CORROBORATION AT ALL. <<<  It occurs exactly once in the whole
!   volume OCR -- here -- and nowhere in docs/ocr/'s manuals, and
!   nothing references it, so the oracle can never fail on it.  The
!   final C rests on ink and on the YSFBCR analogy, and what "LCR"
!   stands for is unknown; see the report.
! * YSFIC is corroborated six times outside this page: printed p.110
!   prints "SIC,YSFIC" at 215031.00, 215032.00, 215042.00,
!   215043.00, 215044.00 and 215046.00 -- Store Instruction Counter
!   into YSFIC, which is what a VF,0 half word is for -- and
!   decks/mcp_bootstrap_p110.strap already carries the name at this
!   address.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! Externals, with the deck that already carries each spelling.
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0              ! p.116 !SYM; p.117/118 SYN
SPROGS  SYN, (8)215021.0              ! p.109/117/118 SYN
SLRPP   SYN, (8)215266.0              ! p.116 line 18 defines it
SLRBU   SYN, (8)215324.0              ! p.116 !SYM; p.117 SYN
SBNDRS  SYN, (8)215224.0              ! p.116 !SYM; p.117 SYN
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0              ! p.128 "K SUPP NOP,K COMM R"
WLODE   SYN, (8)216333.0              ! p.112/p.113 decks "B,W LODE"
YUXSAV  SYN, (8)231363.0              ! THIS tail's YUXSAV -- see above
SL      SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.04       ! p.103 line 14 -LEVEL OF INSTR
SSPFIX  SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.13       ! p.103 line 20 -ON IF PP IN SPECIAL
STSBIT  SYN(BU,1), (8)215001.14       ! p.103 line 21 -ON IF TS STACKED
SAS     SYN(BU,1), .25                ! p.109 line  8 -AUTO STACK STATUS

! An external back-derived from a printed branch or an LVI is pinned
! only to the HALF WORD: bit offsets 0-31 all encode identically, so
! the ".0" on STLR, SPROGS, SLRPP, SLRBU, SBNDRS, KSUPP, WLODE and
! YUXSAV is a CONVENTION and no !CHECK below can test it.  Bit 32
! IS checked, which is why writing ".0" is safe to do and safe to
! check.  SL, SSPFIX, STSBIT and SAS are different: a BB/BZB prints
! the bit offset in the half word's 18-23 field, so lines 39, 40,
! 41 and 47 do check those four to the BIT.

        SLC, (8)216565.40             ! ASSERTED, not printed -- see above

        CNOP                          ! line  1
YINDF   (AA)DD(BU,32),DF  A           ! line  2
YINLC   (AA)DD(BU,32),LC  A           ! line  3
YINPF   (AA)DD(BU,32), PF A           ! line  4
YINZD   (AA)DD(BU,32), ZD A           ! line  5
YINIR   (AA)DD(BU,32), IR A           ! line  6
YINLS   (AA)DD(BU,32), LS A           ! line  7
YINPSH  (AA)DD(BU,32), PSHA           ! line  8
YINXPF  (AA)DD(BU,32),XPFPA           ! line  9
YINXPO  (AA)DD(BU,32), XPOA           ! line 10
YINXPH  (AA)DD(BU,32), XPHA           ! line 11
YINXPL  (AA)DD(BU,32), XPLA           ! line 12
YINZM   (AA)DD(BU,32), ZM A           ! line 13
YINRU   (AA)DD(BU,32), RU A           ! line 14
YINTF   (AA)DD(BU,32), TF A           ! line 15
YINUF   (AA)DD(BU,32), UF A           ! line 16
YINVF   (AA)DD(BU,32), VF A           ! line 17
YINXF   (AA)DD(BU,32), XF A           ! line 18
YINBTR  (AA)DD(BU,32), BTRA           ! line 19
YINDTR  (AA)DD(BU,32), DTRA           ! line 20 (location carries an asterisk)
YINPG0  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG0A           ! line 21
YINPG1  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG1A           ! line 22
YINPG2  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG2A           ! line 23
YINPG3  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG3A           ! line 24
YINPG4  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG4A           ! line 25
YINPG5  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG5A           ! line 26
YINPG6  (AA)DD(BU,32), PG6A           ! line 27
YINXPU  (AA)DD(BU,32), XPUA           ! line 28
        CNOP                          ! line 29
YSFIC   VF,0                          ! line 30
YSFBCR  SYN,SBNDRS                    ! line 31  prints "B ,31 ,01"
YSFLOR  SYN,YUXSAV                    ! line 32  prints "BU,100,10"; the O per printed p.442
!                                       line 33  ***** SPECIAL INTERRUPT
!                                                ROUTINE FOR TS *****
!                                       line 34  (blank comment card)
JWLODE  TI,16,3.0,STLR                ! line 35
        TI,13,19.0,STLR+16.0          ! line 36
        BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101     ! line 37 -STM(U),STLR+1.0 SAVE $MR
        BOPZ,$+.32                    ! line 38 -FOR LASL  LRL
        BB,SL,JWLOD3                  ! line 39 -BR. IF MCP LEVEL
        BB,SSPFIX,JWLOD4              ! line 40 -IF NOW IN SPECIAL FIXUP
        BZB,SPROGS+SAS,WLODE+2.0      ! line 41 -IF NOT AUTOSTACKED
        SR,$15,$1                     ! line 42 (location carries an asterisk)
        SV,$1,0                       ! line 43
        BZXVZ,WLODE+2.0               ! line 44 -LET HIM HAVE IT
JWLOD2  CM1111(BU,1),SLRPP+8.4        ! line 45 -PUT TS IN PP BUFFER
        B,KSUPP                       ! line 46
JWLOD4  CM1111(BU,1),STSBIT           ! line 47 -SAVE TS WHILE IN SPECIAL
        B,KSUPP                       ! line 48
JWLOD3  CM1111(BU,1),SLRBU+8.4        ! line 49 -PUT TS IN BACKUP BUFFER
        B,KSUPP                       ! line 50

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, AS THE ORACLE READS IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Thirty-four symbols and nineteen rows.  The thirty-four cover
! every name the page defines; the nineteen cover every row the page
! prints a BINARY OUTPUT for.  Lines 2-28 print none (see above),
! lines 31-32 are SYNs whose printed LOCATION is a resolved VALUE
! and not storage, and lines 33-34 are comment cards.

!SYM   YINDF    216566.00
!SYM   YINLC    216566.40
!SYM   YINPF    216567.00
!SYM   YINZD    216567.40
!SYM   YINIR    216570.00
!SYM   YINLS    216570.40
!SYM   YINPSH   216571.00
!SYM   YINXPF   216571.40
!SYM   YINXPO   216572.00
!SYM   YINXPH   216572.40
!SYM   YINXPL   216573.00
!SYM   YINZM    216573.40
!SYM   YINRU    216574.00
!SYM   YINTF    216574.40
!SYM   YINUF    216575.00
!SYM   YINVF    216575.40
!SYM   YINXF    216576.00
!SYM   YINBTR   216576.40
!SYM   YINDTR   216577.00
!SYM   YINPG0   216577.40
!SYM   YINPG1   216600.00
!SYM   YINPG2   216600.40
!SYM   YINPG3   216601.00
!SYM   YINPG4   216601.40
!SYM   YINPG5   216602.00
!SYM   YINPG6   216602.40
!SYM   YINXPU   216603.00
!SYM   YSFIC    216604.00
!SYM   YSFBCR   215224.00
!SYM   YSFLOR   231363.00
!SYM   JWLODE   216604.40
!SYM   JWLOD2   216614.00
!SYM   JWLOD4   216615.40
!SYM   JWLOD3   216617.00

!CHECK 216565.40 | 000000.30 00 | line  1 CNOP -- the counter arrives here from printed p.133, which is NOT transcribed; the SLC above asserts it
!CHECK 216603.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 29 CNOP
!CHECK 216604.00 | 000000.00+ | line 30 YSFIC VF,0 -- printed "VF,C"; the value field settles it as 0
!CHECK 216604.40 | 000003.00 80 215230.00 A0 | line 35 JWLODE TI,16,3.0,STLR
!CHECK 216605.40 | 000023.00 80 215250.32 A0 | line 36 TI,13,19.0,STLR+16.0 -- the +16 is DECIMAL and lands 0o20 words on
!CHECK 216606.40 | 215231.47 A0 | line 37 BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101 -- a parenthetical integer entry (C28-6129 p.25) ORs 111101 with its rightmost bit at 26; the comment calls the result "STM(U),STLR+1.0 SAVE $MR"
!CHECK 216607.00 | 216607.47 C6 | line 38 BOPZ,$+.32 -- BOPZ, not BCPZ; BCPZ is rejected by strap_asm and BOPZ gives this printed word
!CHECK 216607.40 | 215001.04 80 216617.34 02 | line 39 BB,SL,JWLOD3 -- the .04 checks SL to the BIT
!CHECK 216610.40 | 215001.13 80 216615.74 02 | line 40 BB,SSPFIX,JWLOD4 -- .13 checks SSPFIX to the bit; 216615.74 is JWLOD4 at .40 (bit 18 set)
!CHECK 216611.40 | 215021.31 80 216335.34 00 | line 41 BZB,SPROGS+SAS,WLODE+2.0 -- .31 checks SAS to the bit
!CHECK 216612.40 | 000021.37 70 | line 42 SR,$15,$1 -- $1 resolves to word 0o21 (location carries an asterisk)
!CHECK 216613.00 | 000000.03 30 | line 43 SV,$1,0
!CHECK 216613.40 | 216335.31 40 | line 44 BZXVZ,WLODE+2.0
!CHECK 216614.00 | 215276.04 80 001000.36 F0 | line 45 JWLOD2 CM1111(BU,1),SLRPP+8.4
!CHECK 216615.00 | 216242.10 00 | line 46 B,KSUPP
!CHECK 216615.40 | 215001.14 80 001000.36 F0 | line 47 JWLOD4 CM1111(BU,1),STSBIT -- .14 checks STSBIT to the bit
!CHECK 216616.40 | 216242.10 00 | line 48 B,KSUPP
!CHECK 216617.00 | 215334.04 80 001000.36 F0 | line 49 JWLOD3 CM1111(BU,1),SLRBU+8.4
!CHECK 216620.00 | 216242.10 00 | line 50 B,KSUPP -- LAST ROW. printed p.135 line 8 prints "216620.40 *  SLC,$", an SLC that emits nothing, so its LOCATION is the counter leaving this page: 216620.00 + one half word. The forward join is closed and no check here consumes it.
